From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mcla-x86 SDK patch layer
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0812: stencil_transfer_cut: the stencil-bit draws of a depth / stencil ownership transfer leave out what the draw rewrites (Direct3D 12 without a stencil reference output; native stream, zero-copy P2)

Source: Ours, written for this SDK (native stream; design note scratch/zerocopy/DESIGN.md section P2 "S1"). Written without a build
  or a run: checked with clang++ 20.1.8 -fsyntax-only (the SDK's Release flags) of pipeline/render_target/cache.cpp,
  d3d12/render_target_cache.cpp and vulkan/render_target_cache.cpp (the changed header); 0 errors, no warning on an added line.
  Needs 0811 (and 0810). Applies after 0780, and also on top of 0800.
Licence: GPL-3 (owner's own work, part of mcla-x86); the patched files are ReXGlue SDK code (BSD-3-Clause)
Purpose: Without a pixel-shader stencil reference output (D3D12_FEATURE_DATA_D3D12_OPTIONS::PSSpecifiedStencilRefSupported false:
  this NVIDIA GPU) the Direct3D 12 backend makes every depth / stencil ownership transfer as one depth draw, a stencil clear and 8
  draws that each set one stencil bit (render_target_cache.cpp: need_stencil_bit_draws, the `j <= is_stencil_bit * 7` loop). When
  the draw that needs the transfer rewrites the stencil of every sample of a rectangle, those 8 draws (and the clear) need not cover
  it. Proof, from the state the host uses for a rectangle list (pipeline_cache.cpp: not polygonal, so the front face's ops and
  write mask serve both faces): RB_DEPTHCONTROL stencil_enable, stencilfunc ALWAYS, a depth test that cannot fail (z off or
  ALWAYS: no depth-fail op can run), stencilzpass REPLACE, RB_STENCILREFMASK stencilwritemask 0xFF; and the coverage of
  GetOverwrittenRectangle with depth_stencil_passes_all (the proof skip_overwritten_transfers and tonemap_transfer_skip use: a
  rectangle list, no user clip planes, no kill / alpha test / alpha to mask, the covered rectangle in guest pixels, the
  half-pixel shift at a draw scale above 1 taken into account). The title's tone map draw meets it (logged RB_DEPTHCONTROL
  0x00708761: stencil on, z off, ALWAYS, REPLACE; RB_STENCILREFMASK 0x00FFFF00: mask 0xFF), so its depth / stencil target's
  transfers (3 a frame at 2000p, 24 stencil-bit draws) bring only the depth plus the strips the quad does not cover. The depth
  draw is unchanged. New cvars ("GPU", hot reload, default false): stencil_transfer_cut, stencil_transfer_cut_poison (the left-out
  stencil filled with 0xA5 after the transfers; the draw must rewrite it). Log every 10 s while on: `[stencil-transfer-cut] ...
  draws ... had their stencil cut, N not (<reason x count>...); stencil-bit transfers left out ... made over a smaller area ...,
  made whole ...; X host Mpx of stencil-bit passes saved`. The cut is for the draw's own target and transfers only
  (last_update_transfers()[0], reset at every Update); resolve clears and clear rectangle draws keep their own cut. Off = no change.
Bucket: REDO

0812-stencil-transfer-cut.patch (mcla-x86 native stream, zero-copy P2).

---
diff --git a/include/rex/graphics/pipeline/render_target/cache.h b/include/rex/graphics/pipeline/render_target/cache.h
index baa1824..d20f78c 100644
--- a/include/rex/graphics/pipeline/render_target/cache.h
+++ b/include/rex/graphics/pipeline/render_target/cache.h
@@ -648,6 +648,21 @@ class RenderTargetCache {
   // The rectangle of all the render targets of the last update that its draw
   // rewrites completely (not to be transferred into), as the clear rectangle
   // of the transfers (a cutout), or null if there isn't one.
+  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0812): stencil_transfer_cut. For the draw being set up (Update), a rectangle of the depth / stencil
+  // target whose stencil the draw rewrites in every sample (a rectangle list covering it, the stencil test ALWAYS, the
+  // depth test unable to fail, the pass operation REPLACE, the write mask 0xFF): the transfers of that target need not
+  // bring its stencil there. Valid only for the transfers of last_update_transfers()[0] made right after the Update (the
+  // backend checks the vector), reset at the start of every Update; the backend that writes the stencil apart from the
+  // depth (Direct3D 12 without a pixel-shader stencil reference output: a draw for each stencil bit) cuts those draws to
+  // it and reports what it did with NoteStencilTransferCut.
+  Transfer::Rectangle transfer_stencil_cutout_ = {};
+  bool transfer_stencil_cutout_valid_ = false;
+  static bool IsStencilTransferCutPoison();
+  // transfers_dropped: stencil-bit invocations left out (all of their rectangles inside the cut), transfers_cut: made over
+  // fewer rectangles, transfers_kept: made whole; pixel_passes_saved: host pixels times the 8 passes.
+  void NoteStencilTransferCut(uint32_t transfers_dropped, uint32_t transfers_cut, uint32_t transfers_kept,
+                              uint64_t pixel_passes_saved);
+
   // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0811): transfer_census_log. transfer_census_reason_ (private) says why the transfers that
   // ChangeOwnership finds next are what they are (cut by which skip, or kept and why), set before it by the draw, the
   // clear rectangle draw and the resolve clear; the transfers a cut leaves out whole are counted there, the backend counts
